extract_result.purpose:
This Departmental Regulation (DR) establishes the processes required to develop the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) Information Technology (IT) Strategic Plan in accordance with:

a. The Clinger-Cohen Act of 1996, 40 United States Code (U.S.C.) Section 11101, et seq.;

b. The Government Performance and Results Modernization Act of 2010, Public Law (P.L.) § 111-352;

c. The Federal Information Technology Acquisition Reform Act (FITARA), P.L. 113-291 §§ 831-837;

d. The Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995, 44 U.S.C. § 3501, et seq.;

e. Federal Agency Responsibilities, 44 U.S.C. § 3506(b)(2);

f. Performance and Results-based Management, 40 U.S.C. § 11313;

g. Chief Information Officer, 7 Code of Federal Regulations (CFR) § 2.32;

h. Office of Management and Budget (OMB), Circular A-11 Revised, Preparing, Submitting, and Executing the Budget;

i. OMB, Circular A-130, Management of Federal Information Resources; and

j. OMB, Memorandum M-15-14, Management and Oversight of Federal Information Technology.
